## Thread.Abort → Cooperative Cancellation Migration

### Pattern Analysis

Your code contains **three** patterns that must change for .NET 8:

| Pattern Found | Location | Issue on .NET 8 |
|---|---|---|
| `Thread.Abort()` | `Stop()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` |
| `catch (ThreadAbortException)` | `ProcessLoop()` | Never thrown — cleanup never runs |
| `Thread.ResetAbort()` | `ProcessLoop()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` |

### Migrated Code

```csharp
public class BackgroundProcessor : IDisposable
{
    private Thread? _workerThread;
    private CancellationTokenSource? _cts;

    public void Start()
    {
        _cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
        var token = _cts.Token;
        _workerThread = new Thread(() => ProcessLoop(token));
        _workerThread.IsBackground = true;
        _workerThread.Start();
    }

    private void ProcessLoop(CancellationToken token)
    {
        while (!token.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            try
            {
                var item = GetNextItem(token); // pass token to unblock
                ProcessItem(item);
            }
            catch (OperationCanceledException) when (token.IsCancellationRequested)
            {
                // Clean up partial work — replaces ThreadAbortException catch
                RollbackCurrentTransaction();
            }
            finally
            {
                FlushBuffers();
            }
        }
    }

    public void Stop()
    {
        _cts?.Cancel(); // signals cooperative cancellation

        // Wait with a timeout instead of Thread.Sleep + Abort
        if (_workerThread != null && _workerThread.IsAlive)
        {
            if (!_workerThread.Join(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2)))
            {
                // Thread didn't stop — it's stuck in uncooperative code.
                // Log a warning. Cannot force-kill a managed thread in .NET 8.
            }
        }
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Stop();
        _cts?.Dispose();
    }
}
```

### Critical Change: `GetNextItem` Must Cooperate

If `GetNextItem()` blocks (e.g., on a `BlockingCollection` or socket), cancellation **will stall** until it unblocks. You must pass the token through:

```csharp
// Before (.NET Framework) — blocks indefinitely, relied on Abort to interrupt
private WorkItem GetNextItem()
{
    return _queue.Take(); // blocks forever if queue is empty
}

// After (.NET 8) — wakes up when cancelled
private WorkItem GetNextItem(CancellationToken token)
{
    return _queue.Take(token); // throws OperationCanceledException
}
```

### Key Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| **Not passing token to blocking calls** | `CancellationToken` can't interrupt `Thread.Sleep` or blocking I/O. Replace `Thread.Sleep(ms)` with `token.WaitHandle.WaitOne(ms)`. |
| **Not disposing `CancellationTokenSource`** | Leaks timers/callbacks. The `IDisposable` pattern above handles this. |
| **Swallowing `OperationCanceledException`** | The `when (token.IsCancellationRequested)` filter ensures you only catch *your* cancellation, not an unrelated one. |
| **Assuming cancellation is immediate** | It's cooperative — only works at checkpoints. If `ProcessItem()` is long-running, add `token.ThrowIfCancellationRequested()` inside it. |
| **No fallback for stuck threads** | .NET 8 has **no** `Thread.Abort` equivalent. If code can't cooperate, move it to a child `Process` and use `Process.Kill()`. |

### What Changed and Why

| .NET Framework | .NET 8 | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `volatile bool _running` | `CancellationToken` | Token integrates with blocking APIs; a bool can't wake a blocked thread |
| `Thread.Abort()` | `CancellationTokenSource.Cancel()` | Abort throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` |
| `catch (ThreadAbortException)` | `catch (OperationCanceledException)` | ThreadAbortException is never thrown |
| `Thread.ResetAbort()` | Removed — not needed | Cooperative model doesn't auto-rethrow |
| `Thread.Sleep(2000)` then Abort | `_workerThread.Join(2000)` | Join actually waits for the thread; Sleep just delays |
